.TH MOKUTIL 1 "Thu Jul 25 2013"
.SH NAME

mokutil \- utility to manipulate machine owner keys

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmokutil\fR [--list-enrolled | -l]
        ([--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--list-new | -N]
        ([--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--list-delete | -D]
        ([--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--import \fIkeylist\fR| -i \fIkeylist\fR]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P] |
         [--mokx | -X] | [--ca-check] | [--ignore-keyring])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--import-list \fImanifest\fR]
        ([--policy \fIpolicyfile\fR] | [--no-policy])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--delete \fIkeylist\fR | -d \fIkeylist\fR]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P] |
         [--mokx |- X] | [--policy \fIpolicyfile\fR] | [--no-policy])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--revoke-import]
        ([--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--revoke-delete]
        ([--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--export | -x]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--password | -p]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--clear-password | -c]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--disable-validation]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--enable-validation]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--sb-state]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--test-key \fIkeyfile\fR | -t \fIkeyfile\fR]
        ([--mokx | -X] | [--ca-check] | [--ignore-keyring])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--reset]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P] |
         [--mok | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--generate-hash=\fIpassword\fR | -g\fIpassword\fR]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--ignore-db]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--use-db]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--import-hash \fIhash\fR]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P] |
         [--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--delete-hash \fIhash\fR]
        ([--hash-file \fIhashfile\fR | -f \fIhashfile\fR] | [--root-pw | -P] |
         [--mokx | -X])
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--set-verbosity (\fItrue\fR | \fIfalse\fR)]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--set-fallback-verbosity (\fItrue\fR | \fIfalse\fR)]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--set-fallback-noreboot (\fItrue\fR | \fIfalse\fR)]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--pk]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--kek]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--db]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--dbx]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--list-sbat-revocations]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--set-sbat-policy (\fIlatest\fR | \fIprevious\fR | \fIdelete\fR)]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--timeout \fI-1,0..0x7fff\fR]
.br
\fBmokutil\fR [--policy-check \fIpolicyfile\fR]
.br

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmokutil\fR is a tool to import or delete the machines owner keys
(MOK) stored in the database of shim.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-l, --list-enrolled\fR
List the keys the already stored in the database
.TP
\fB-N, --list-new\fR
List the keys to be enrolled
.TP
\fB-D, --list-delete\fR
List the keys to be deleted
.TP
\fB-i, --import\fR
Collect the following files and form an enrolling request to shim. The files must
be in DER format.
.TP
\fB--import-list \fImanifest\fR\fR
Read DER key paths from \fImanifest\fR and form one enrolling request. Blank
lines and lines beginning with \fB#\fR are ignored. Relative paths are resolved
from the manifest directory. A directory entry expands to the regular files in
that directory. The whole batch is validated before any request is written.
.TP
\fB-d, --delete\fR
Collect the following files and form a deleting request to shim. The files must be
in DER format.
.TP
\fB--revoke-import\fR
Revoke the current import request (MokNew)
.TP
\fB--revoke-delete\fR
Revoke the current delete request (MokDel)
.TP
\fB-x, --export\fR
Export the keys stored in MokListRT
.TP
\fB-p, --password\fR
Setup the password for MokManager (MokPW)
.TP
\fB-c, --clear-password\fR
Clear the password for MokManager (MokPW)
.TP
\fB--disable-validation\fR
Disable the validation process in shim
.TP
\fB--enable-validation\fR
Enable the validation process in shim
.TP
\fB--sb-state\fR
Show SecureBoot State
.TP
\fB-t, --test-key\fR
Test if the key is enrolled or not
.TP
\fB--reset\fR
Reset MOK list
.TP
\fB--generate-hash\fR
Generate the password hash
.TP
\fB--hash-file\fR
Use the password hash from a specific file
.TP
\fB-P, --root-pw\fR
Use the root password hash from /etc/shadow
.TP
\fB--ignore-db\fR
Tell shim to not use the keys in db to verify EFI images
.TP
\fB--use-db\fR
Tell shim to use the keys in db to verify EFI images (default)
.TP
\fB-X, --mokx\fR
Manipulate the MOK blacklist (MOKX) instead of the MOK list
.TP
\fB--import-hash\fR
Create an enrolling request for the hash of a key in DER format. Note that
this is not the password hash.
.TP
\fB--delete-hash\fR
Create a deleting request for the hash of a key in DER format. Note that
this is not the password hash.
.TP
\fB--set-verbosity\fR
Set the SHIM_VERBOSE to make shim more or less verbose
.TP
\fB--set-fallback-verbosity\fR
Set the FALLBACK_VERBOSE to make fallback more or less verbose
.TP
\fB--set-fallback-noreboot\fR
Set the FB_NO_REBOOT to prevent fallback from automatically rebooting the system
.TP
\fB--pk\fR
List the keys in the public Platform Key (PK)
.TP
\fB--kek\fR
List the keys in the Key Exchange Key Signature database (KEK)
.TP
\fB--db\fR
List the keys in the secure boot signature store (db)
.TP
\fB--dbx\fR
List the keys in the secure boot blacklist signature store (dbx)
.TP
\fB--list-sbat-revocations\fR
List the entries in the Secure Boot Advanced Targeting store (SBAT)
.TP
\fB--set-sbat-policy (\fIlatest\fR | \fIprevious\fR | \fIdelete\fR)\fR
Set the SbatPolicy UEFI Variable to have shim apply either the latest
or the previous SBAT revocations.  If UEFI Secure Boot is disabled, then
delete will reset the SBAT revocations to an empty revocation list.
While latest and previous are persistent configuration, delete will be
cleared by shim on the next boot whether or not it succeeds. The default
behavior is for shim to apply the previous revocations.
.TP
\fB--timeout\fR
Set the timeout for MOK prompt
.TP
\fB--ca-check\fR
Check if the CA of the given key is already enrolled or blocked in the key
databases.
.TP
\fB--ignore-keyring\fR
Ignore the kernel builtin trusted keys keyring check when enrolling a key into MokList
.TP
\fB--policy \fIpolicyfile\fR\fR
Apply the import, delete, revoke, and reset policy in \fIpolicyfile\fR. If this
option is omitted, \fBMOKUTIL_POLICY\fR is used when set, otherwise
\fB/etc/mokutil/policy.conf\fR is used when it exists. Without any policy file,
\fBmokutil\fR keeps its legacy behavior.
.TP
\fB--no-policy\fR
Disable policy discovery for this invocation.
.TP
\fB--policy-check \fIpolicyfile\fR\fR
Validate \fIpolicyfile\fR, print its effective rules, and exit. This does not
access EFI variables.

.SH POLICY FILE
Policy files use one directive per line. Both \fBkey value\fR and
\fBkey = value\fR forms are accepted. Lines beginning with \fB#\fR are
comments. Unknown or duplicate scalar directives, malformed values, missing
versions, and directly conflicting certificate rules are rejected.

The required directive is:
.TP
\fBversion 1\fR
Selects the only currently supported policy format.

.PP
Operation directives default to \fBdeny\fR when a policy is enabled:
.TP
\fBimport allow|deny\fR
Allow or deny certificate import into MokNew or MokXNew.
.TP
\fBdelete allow|deny\fR
Allow or deny certificate deletion requests.
.TP
\fBrevoke-import allow|deny\fR
Allow or deny revocation of a pending import request.
.TP
\fBrevoke-delete allow|deny\fR
Allow or deny revocation of a pending delete request.
.TP
\fBrevoke allow|deny\fR
Shorthand that sets both revoke directives.
.TP
\fBreset allow|deny\fR
Allow or deny reset of the complete MOK or MOKX request.

.PP
Additional directives:
.TP
\fBmax-batch \fInumber\fR\fR
Limit the number of files in one import or delete batch. The range is 1 to 4096;
the default is 64.
.TP
\fBrequire-ca yes|no\fR
Require imported certificates to be CA certificates. The default is \fBno\fR.
.TP
\fBallow-path \fIpath\fR\fR
Require key files to be below \fIpath\fR. The path must be absolute and must
exist when the policy is loaded. The directive may be repeated.
.TP
\fBdeny-path \fIpath\fR\fR
Reject key files below \fIpath\fR. Deny rules take precedence over allow rules.
.TP
\fBallow-sha256 \fIfingerprint\fR\fR
Allow a certificate by the SHA-256 fingerprint of its DER encoding. When at
least one allow rule is present, other certificates are denied. The directive
may be repeated.
.TP
\fBdeny-sha256 \fIfingerprint\fR\fR
Reject a certificate by its SHA-256 fingerprint. The directive may be repeated.

.PP
When certificate fingerprint rules are present, SHA-256 hash requests are
checked against the same rules. Other hash lengths are rejected by the policy.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# /etc/mokutil/policy.conf
version 1
import allow
delete allow
revoke-import allow
revoke-delete allow
reset deny
max-batch 8
require-ca yes
allow-path /etc/mok/keys

mokutil --policy-check /etc/mokutil/policy.conf
mokutil --policy /etc/mokutil/policy.conf --import-list /etc/mok/keys.list
.fi
.TP
